---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import KnowledgeDemo from '../../components/KnowledgeDemo.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <section class="product-hero-wide">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="product-label">
        <span class="app-icon green" aria-hidden="true">
          ⌕
        </span>{' '}
        CIVOLYN Knowledge
      </p>
      <div class="headline-row">
        <h1>
          Find clarity in everything
          <br />
          <em>your team knows.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="intro-copy">
          The answer may already exist. In a playbook, a project note, a policy.
          Give the good thinking a place to be found.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a href="#preview" class="button button-dark">
          Search the example library <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <span class="disclosure">
          <span class="status-dot"></span> Fictional concept · No connected
          sources or live AI
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    class="container"
    id="preview"
    aria-label="Knowledge interactive preview"
  >
    <div class="full-demo-stage">
      <KnowledgeDemo />
    </div>
    <p class="section-caption">
      <span>
        Six original sample documents. Search, filter and open a source.
      </span>
      <span>Local preview / Knowledge</span>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container product-benefits">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">FROM SCATTERED TO SHARED</p>
        <h2>
          A good answer should
          <br />
          <em>show where it came from.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="numbered-list">
        <li>
          <span class="number">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Search for the thing you need.</h3>
            <p>
              Try a topic like onboarding or review. The example library matches
              words in titles and document text, then narrows results by
              category.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="number">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Keep the source in sight.</h3>
            <p>
              Open a result to read its prepared snippet and source reference. A
              confident-sounding answer should never replace the opportunity to
              inspect the original context.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="number">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Organise by how people work.</h3>
            <p>
              Guides explain a practice. Projects record a decision. Policies
              set a boundary. Those distinctions help a reader know what kind of
              information they have found.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section dark-section">
    <div class="container split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CONTEXT GOES A LONG WAY</p>
        <h2>
          Not just an answer.
          <br />
          <em>A better starting point.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          A project lead looking for an onboarding checklist needs more than a
          paragraph. They need to know which practice it describes, when it
          applies and who should make the next decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          In the imagined platform, summaries would help people orient
          themselves while references preserve the path back to the source. In
          this website, all snippets are original prepared examples. No
          generated answer is presented as a fact.
        </p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/technology/">
          Read the conceptual AI principles <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">KNOWLEDGE THAT HAS SOMEWHERE TO GO</p>
      <h2>
        Useful at the moment
        <br />
        <em>it becomes relevant.</em>
      </h2>
      <div class="use-case-row">
        <article>
          <h3>Before a new project.</h3>
          <p>
            Find the intake playbook and turn an unclear request into a brief
            the team can actually use.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>During an approval.</h3>
          <p>
            Bring the review policy into view. Separate what has been proposed
            from what has been agreed.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>At the weekly review.</h3>
          <p>
            Read the team practice, revisit the reasoning and record the next
            action with its owner.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-note">
        <p>
          <b>Search without a connection.</b> The six samples are bundled into
          the page. Queries stay in this browser. There is no semantic search
          model, document upload, real source permission system or persistent
          library.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA title="Bring a little more context to the work." />
  <div class="container product-nav">
    <a href="/products/flow/">← Previous: Flow</a>
    <a href="/products/signal/">Next: Signal ↗</a>
  </div>
</Layout>
